      "description": "Changes recorded by each PE service, counted per bar over the range. **Whole events rather than a rate**: console change is rare and bursty, so a per-second figure reads as 0.002 and tells nobody anything. **Read the shape rather than the value**: console change is normally near zero, so a step is somebody working and a flat line is a console nobody has touched. The underlying series counts every change since the install was built, which is why it is drawn as a rate \u2014 the raw total is the age of the installation as much as anything. **What this cannot tell you is what changed**, because the activity API has no time filter and the breakdown would cost a walk of the entire history every poll; the console itself is where a specific change is read.",
