      "description": "Authentication tokens created and revoked, counted per bar over the range. **Read the pair rather than either line**: tokens are meant to be minted, and a mint rate on its own says only that the estate is being used. Generation consistently above revocation is tokens accumulating, which is how a long-lived credential nobody remembers issuing comes to exist. Counted forward from the pdctng daemon's start, so a restart shows as a gap rather than as a lull.",
