    {
      "title": "Recent activity, in full",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 89
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Not collected yet, and it will not arrive as a metric.** The panels above are counts, which Prometheus is good at. The events themselves carry a subject, an object, a timestamp and an address, which Prometheus is bad at and a log store is built for.\n\npdctng already runs Loki on this node for PE's own logs where `enable_logs` is on, so the home for the detail exists. Expected here: a log panel over the activity events, filtered by service and by event type, sitting under the counts that tell you which day to look at.\n\n**Whether source IP addresses are collected at all is open.** They are the most identifying field in the payload and the least often needed, and dropping them at collection is a decision somebody should take on purpose rather than by default."
      },
      "id": 1319770990
    },
